#
# The @lua* commands below aren't Doxygen commands at all - they're read by
# this repo's own scripts/generate_lua_api_docs.py, which builds the Lua-
# facing docs/lua-api pages straight from these same source comments (see
# CLAUDE.md's "Lua API docs" plan). Registering them here just keeps
# Doxygen's own C++ reference from warning about "unknown command" wherever
# they appear - @luaname also gets a small real payoff for the C++ side too,
# rendering the Lua-callable name a method is registered under (something
# this reference otherwise has no way to show at all, since that mapping
# only exists in a runtime lua_register() call - see doxygen.yml's own
# workflow comment). @luagroup/@luacategory/@luaheading carry no meaningful
# text for a C++ reader (they're pure grouping/heading-override keys for
# the generator) so they expand to nothing. @luadoc/@luaexample/@luaoutro
# take no argument - the text that follows any one of them, until the next
# recognized command, is read as plain Doxygen detailed-description text
# same as always; only the generator script gives it different treatment.
#
ALIASES                += luaname{1}="\par Lua-callable as:^^`\1`"
ALIASES                += luagroup{1}=
ALIASES                += luacategory{1}=
ALIASES                += luaheading{1}=
ALIASES                += luadoc=
ALIASES                += luaexample=
ALIASES                += luaoutro=
